{%- if lcp -%}
<a class="u-url sr-only" href="{{ page.url }}">{{ title }}</a>{% comment %} Visual fix: sr-only so the permalink's own title isn't printed twice (h1 above already carries p-name) — see types/article.liquid's comment. {% endcomment %}
{%- if date %}<time class="dt-published" datetime="{{ date | isoInstant }}">{{ date | humanDate }}</time>{% endif %}
{%- if inReplyTo %}<p>In reply to <a class="u-in-reply-to" href="{{ inReplyTo }}">{{ inReplyTo }}</a></p>{% endif %}
{%- comment %} Task 18 (§7.4): see types/article.liquid for why h2,h3. {% endcomment -%}
<div class="content-grid e-content"><heading-anchors selector="h2,h3">{{ content }}</heading-anchors></div>
{%- else -%}
{%- comment %} Task (visual fix, corrected from the prior S4 pass): a reply
is titleless by IndieWeb design (see types/note.liquid for the fallback
label / visible-link-text reasoning). Its own words, if it has any, are its
substance — same truncated/stripped treatment, now as the visible
`.posts-link` text instead of a hidden anchor plus a separate paragraph. A
reply can be contentless (just a share of the target, nothing of its own to
say), so fall back to the reply target's own text — matching bookmark's
`{{ title | default: bookmarkOf }}` convention, plain text rather than a
second nested `<a>` (invalid inside the outer anchor). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign replyWords = content | strip_html | truncate: 70 -%}
<a class="posts-link p-name u-url" href="{{ page.url }}">{{ replyWords | default: inReplyTo }}</a>
<span class="tags"></span>
{%- if date %}<time class="date dt-published" datetime="{{ date | isoInstant }}">{{ date | humanDate }}</time>{% endif %}
{%- endif -%}
